

**20.7.11**: \(K_{\rm i}(z,t)\)=\(Z_{\nu}^{(0)}(u)[M(z,t)]^{-\nu\tau}\), \(s\) any integer. See 20.4.7 for definition of \(Z_{\nu}^{(t)}\)+\(z_{\nu+2s}(u)\).

From the known expansions for \(Z_{\nu}^{(t)}\)+\(z_{\rm d}(u)\) when \({\cal D}z\) is large and positive it may be verified that 20.7.12**: \(M_{\nu}^{(t)}(z,q)\)=

\[\frac{(-1)^{s}}{\pi\varepsilon_{\rm i}}\int_{0}^{\tau}Z_{\nu+2s}^{(0)}(u)\left[ \frac{\cosh\,z+it}{\cosh\,z-it}\right]^{-\nu-s}F_{\nu}(t)dt\]

where \(M_{\nu}^{(t)}(z,q)\) is given by 20.4.12, \(s\)=0, 1, .

